posals rest on observations from fewer than 20 packets rather than on findings. It also flags the version gap (TEP-0006) and the drop in permission denials that the method never recorded, and leaves both for the human to decide.\n\n**Weaknesses that don't block approval**\n1. **TEP-0007's starting figure is too high.** Its hypothesis starts from \"11 of 27\" blocked or discarded records. That counts every blocked or discarded record, including external blocks that have nothing to do with placeholders or narrow targets, such as PKT-0057, 0063 and 0066. Using it as the starting point makes the target easier to hit than it should be. AUD-4 should count only the records whose cause matches.\n2. **TEP-0003 is half-decided.** The audit says \"not supported\" and then makes keeping it depend on TEP-0008. That is reasonable, but it leaves the TEP open.\n3. **The packet's \"Lessons for the Atlas\" section is empty.** The two lessons appear only in the final report: changes made outside the method should be recorded and versioned, and packets should be sliced better when issued. Someone should copy them into the packet or the Atlas at integration.\n4. **`theseus validate` gave 1 warning that the executor did not look into.** I don't know what it is, and it did not stop the factory's checks.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Audit report and two well-formed TEPs meet the goal within contract; outcome counts check out, and the weaknesses are minor (TEP-0007 starting figure, Atlas lessons not copied into the packet)","ttft_ms":2278,"type":"result","duration_ms":28831,"uuid":"2143872a-2c11-498e-928c-651cf4fb78e0","ttft_stream_ms":892,"time_to_request_ms":387,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":240,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request